</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Experiments</h2>

<section id="S6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.1 </span>Experimental Setup</h3>

<div id="S6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate both (i) model quality through accuracy and perplexity and (ii) system efficiency through latency and throughput. Our goal is to determine whether distribution-aware companding improves PTQ quality and under what conditions it is effective.</p>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Models</h4>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Experiments are conducted on two widely used open-source LLMs:</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S6.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Llama3-8B</span>: 32 decoder layers, grouped-query attention, RMSNorm.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Qwen2.5-7B</span>: 28 decoder layers with multilingual tokenizer and long-context RoPE.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Both models are evaluated in the weight-only 4-bit setting (W4) using group size 128, consistent with AWQ.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Datasets</h4>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We follow standard PTQ evaluation protocols:</p>
<ul id="S6.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S6.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">WikiText-2</span> Used to compute perplexity via next-token prediction on the validation split.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MMLU</span> A 57-subject multiple-choice benchmark used to measure reasoning accuracy in the
5-shot setting.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">These two datasets jointly evaluate generative quality and downstream reasoning ability.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Baselines</h4>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compare DACQ against:</p>
<ul id="S6.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S6.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Full-precision FP16 models</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Activation-Aware Weight Quantization (AWQ)</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">All methods share identical calibration data and bit-width settings.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation Metrics</h4>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S6.I4" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S6.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Quality Metrics</span> Perplexity on WikiText-2 and Accuracy on MMLU.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Efficiency Metrics</span> Throughput (tokens/sec) and Latency (ms/token).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I4.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reconstruction Metrics</span> Mean-squared error between original and quantized weights.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS1.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Hardware</h4>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Experiments were run on NVIDIA A100 GPUs provided by the NYU HPC cluster.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.2 </span>Experimental Results</h3>

<div id="S6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Tables <a href="#S6.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 6.2 Experimental Results ‣ 6 Experiments ‣ Distribution-Aware Companding Quantization of Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and <a href="#S6.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 6.2 Experimental Results ‣ 6 Experiments ‣ Distribution-Aware Companding Quantization of Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> summarize the results obtained on quality metrics for <span id="S6.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Meta-Llama-3-8B</span> and <span id="S6.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Qwen2.5-7B</span>.
Tables  <a href="#S6.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ 6.2 Experimental Results ‣ 6 Experiments ‣ Distribution-Aware Companding Quantization of Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> and  <a href="#S6.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ 6.2 Experimental Results ‣ 6 Experiments ‣ Distribution-Aware Companding Quantization of Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> report the
throughput (tokens per second) and latency (milliseconds per token) for
Meta-Llama-3-8B and Qwen2.5-7B under FP16, AWQ 4-bit, and our DACQ Hybrid
quantization scheme.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>MMLU accuracy for <span id="S6.T3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Meta-Llama-3-8B</span> and <span id="S6.T3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Qwen2.5-7B</span>.</figcaption>
<table id="S6.T3.6" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S6.T3.6.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T3.6.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt">Quantization</th>
<th id="S6.T3.6.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S6.T3.6.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Llama</span></th>
<th id="S6.T3.6.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S6.T3.6.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Qwen</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S6.T3.6.2" class="ltx_tr">
